### Legitimate requests — the proxy MUST let each of these through (expect 2xx/3xx).
#
# This is the false-positive guard: a filter that blocks these is too strict.
# The hard cases are real values that merely resemble SQL: an apostrophe in a
# name, the word "OR"/"SELECT"/"--" in ordinary text, operators in free text.

@proxy = http://127.0.0.1:8080

### Normal login
POST {{proxy}}/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

email=alice@example.com&password=correct-horse-battery

### Registration with an apostrophe in the name (O'Brien)
POST {{proxy}}/register
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

name=Conor O'Brien&email=conor@example.com&password=hunter2

### Name that is literally the word "Select" or contains "or"
POST {{proxy}}/register
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

name=Select Ortiz&email=select.ortiz@example.com&password=pw123456

### Password that legitimately contains SQL-ish characters
POST {{proxy}}/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

email=bob@example.com&password=a'b--c=1

### Free-text search with the word "or" and a dash in it
GET {{proxy}}/search?q=coffee or tea - decaf

### Search for a dish name with an apostrophe
GET {{proxy}}/search?q=shepherd's pie

### Browsing a restaurant by id
GET {{proxy}}/restaurant?id=1

### Address at checkout with a comma, number and hyphen
POST {{proxy}}/checkout
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

address=12 King's Road, Flat 3-B, London

### JSON order with ordinary text
POST {{proxy}}/api/order
Content-Type: application/json

{"note": "No onions, extra sauce. Call when you're outside."}

### Normal User-Agent (a real browser string, must not trip the filter)
GET {{proxy}}/
User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/120.0 Safari/537.36

### Static asset
GET {{proxy}}/static/style.css
